  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "XaWLxDR3Prdo"
   },
   "source": [
    "Write a Python program to find the highest temperature from a list using max()."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "executionInfo": {
     "elapsed": 38,
     "status": "ok",
     "timestamp": 1783942362184,
     "user": {
      "displayName": "Suvarna Thathikalam",
      "userId": "13551707280037048727"
     },
     "user_tz": -330
    },
    "id": "4_Q4khLaPujo",
    "outputId": "a5a519e8-af00-4a9e-f299-fc871168375c"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The highest temperature in a list: 45\n",
      "45\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "temp=(45,37,25,39)\n",
    "res=max(temp)\n",
    "print(\"The highest temperature in a list:\",res)\n",
    "print(res)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
